John Morgan (of Rhiwpera), also known as Sir John Morgan, was a Welsh politician who lived from 4 January 1671 to 7 March 1720. He was the youngest son of Sir William Morgan and his wife, Blanche, who was his cousin. After his elder brother, Sir Thomas Morgan, died without surviving children in 1700, John inherited the family's Tredegar Estate. He entered the House of Commons as a Member of Parliament for Monmouthshire in 1701 and represented it until his death in 1720. 

John inherited Rhiwperra Castle and the manor of Gwynllwg from his uncle, Sir John Morgan, and obtained the lord lieutenancy of the county and Brecknockshire. He had two sons, Sir William Morgan and Sir Thomas Morgan, and a daughter, Martha, who married the 3rd Earl of Oxford. He died in 1720 and was buried at Machen. 

