Frederick, Hereditary Prince of Baden-Durlach, full name Frederick, was a German hereditary prince of the Margraviate of Baden-Durlach. He was born on 7 October 1703 and died on 26 March 1732. Frederick was the son of Charles III William, Margrave of Baden-Durlach, and Magdalena Wilhelmine of Württemberg, who was the daughter of William Louis, Duke of Württemberg. He became heir apparent to the Margraviate of Baden-Durlach when his elder brother, Charles Magnus, died in 1712. However, Frederick died before his father and therefore never assumed governance of Durlach. He served in the imperial army and was appointed colonel in 1724 and major general in 1728. On 3 July 1727, he married Amalia of Nassau-Dietz, the daughter of John William Friso, Prince of Orange. The relevant time period for Frederick's life and lineage spans from the early 18th century to the mid-18th century.
